{
    "_doc": [
        "Shared test vectors for the device type record command grammar (DeviceTypeGrammar in C++ and",
        "DeviceTypeGrammar.py in the generator). Each vector compiles 'str' as 'field' (detection, init or poll) and",
        "must give exactly these steps and issues. A step: write = hex bytes written, read = bytes read, pause = ms",
        "after, checks = alternatives as 'mask:value' hex (detection only; a pause-only value gives one empty check",
        "':'), crc8w = each 2-byte word read followed by a CRC-8, expr = the read length is an r{...} expression.",
        "issues lists issue names in order. A detection string with an error has no steps."
    ],
    "vectors": [
        {"name": "who am i", "field": "detection", "str": "0x0f=0x69,0x6a,0x6c",
         "steps": [{"write": "0f", "read": 1, "pause": 0, "checks": ["ff:69", "ff:6a", "ff:6c"]}], "issues": []},
        {"name": "two byte hex", "field": "detection", "str": "0x07=0x81c4,0x81d4",
         "steps": [{"write": "07", "read": 2, "pause": 0, "checks": ["ffff:81c4", "ffff:81d4"]}], "issues": []},
        {"name": "binary mask", "field": "detection", "str": "0x0c=0b100001100000XXXX",
         "steps": [{"write": "0c", "read": 2, "pause": 0, "checks": ["fff0:8600"]}], "issues": []},
        {"name": "binary with 0x inside (C3 regression)", "field": "detection", "str": "0x86=0b1010XXXX&0x87=0x05",
         "steps": [{"write": "86", "read": 1, "pause": 0, "checks": ["f0:a0"]},
                   {"write": "87", "read": 1, "pause": 0, "checks": ["ff:05"]}], "issues": []},
        {"name": "write pause then read", "field": "detection", "str": "0x00FF=p25&=0bXXXXXXXX00000101",
